# CHANGELOG Maintenance

Update `CHANGELOG.md` when adding, changing, or removing functionality.

## Format

Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) conventions:

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

### Added
- New feature description

### Changed
- Existing feature modification

### Fixed
- Bug fix description

### Removed
- Removed feature description

## [0.11.0] - 2026-07-13

### Added
- ...
```

## Rules

- New entries go under `[Unreleased]` as the change lands
- When releasing, rename `[Unreleased]` to `[X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`, add a fresh `[Unreleased]`
  heading, bump `VERSION` to match, then push and tag `vX.Y.Z` (see `deployment-rules.mdc`).
  The heading uses the bare version; the git tag carries the `v` prefix.
- Write entries from the user's perspective, not implementation details
- Group related changes under one bullet rather than listing every file touched
- Call out anything that requires operator action on upgrade — a new required environment
  variable, a data migration, a changed default — even if the user-facing effect is small
- Reference GitHub issue/PR numbers where applicable
